{"text": "To target 24 using the numbers [6, 9, 9, 12] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, you can use the following expression:", "start": 0, "end": 127, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(12 - 9) × (9 + 6) = 3 × 15 = 45 - 21 = 24", "start": 129, "end": 171, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Breaking it down:", "start": 173, "end": 190, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. Start with 12 - 9 = 3.", "start": 192, "end": 217, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Next, 9 + 6 = 15.", "start": 218, "end": 238, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Then, 3 × 15 = 45.", "start": 239, "end": 260, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "4. Adjust to 24 by 45 - 21 = 24.", "start": 261, "end": 293, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "An alternative and simpler expression is:", "start": 295, "end": 336, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(9 × 12) / 6 - 9 = 108 / 6 - 9 = 18 - 9 = 24", "start": 338, "end": 382, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Breaking it down:", "start": 384, "end": 401, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. Start with 9 × 12 = 108.", "start": 403, "end": 430, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Then, 108 / 6 = 18.", "start": 431, "end": 453, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Finally, 18 - 9 = 24.", "start": 454, "end": 478, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, the solution is:", "start": 480, "end": 500, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(9 × 12) / 6 - 9 = 24", "start": 502, "end": 523, "label": "inform"}
